~ _oakhaven_backup
Backup: Oakhaven Saved Too Late: The village survives in this history. The crater does not. The people rebuild around a hole that keeps asking for names.
Memory Villager: You would preserve us, even when the pain keeps running. Is a saved wound still a saved life?
Memory Villager: You would release us quickly. But some histories need someone to stand nearby when the door opens.
Memory Villager: You would bargain for us. We learned what it costs when safety arrives with terms.
Memory Villager: No record says what you do with people history hurts.
Kaelen: A clean timeline can still leave dirty grief.

~ _ironhold_backup
Backup: Ironhold Without Freedom: Ironhold thrives here. Markets run perfectly. No one starves. No one votes. No one leaves.
Ironhold Clerk: You silenced the Choir. Would you silence this city if freedom could only return through collapse?
Ironhold Clerk: You preserved the Choir as warning. Would you preserve this city as evidence, even while it keeps obeying?
Ironhold Clerk: You rewrote the Choir. Would you rewrite Ironhold too, or admit some citizens may refuse your improved future?
Ironhold Clerk: Order feeds us. Freedom is a rumor with empty hands.
Kaelen: A world can function and still fail everyone inside it.

~ _mirror_city_backup
Backup: Mirror City Without Witnesses: The city reflects every choice, but nobody remains to answer back. Kaelen won every argument because he was the only voice left.
Empty Mirror: You refused obedience. Good. But defiance without witnesses can become a private throne.
Empty Mirror: You refused the perfect rescue. Good. But urgency without witnesses can become damage called progress.
Empty Mirror: You refused abandonment. Good. But staying without witnesses can become ownership.
Empty Mirror: No witness names the self you fear most. The mirror cannot cross-examine silence.
Kaelen: If I am the only person allowed to interpret history, I become SOVEREIGN with a different voice.
